"""
Standard.Ssh against a real sshd: runs the remote command WORD...
on HOST through /usr/bin/ssh, as Standard.Ssh builds it, within MILLIS
milliseconds and MOST bytes of output and of errors.

    sshrun HOST PORT USER MILLIS MOST WORD...

On a run it prints code=N, then the output after a line "output:" and the
errors after a line "errors:", and exits 0 whatever N is.  On a failure of
Standard.Ssh it prints error=BadTarget, NotStarted, CommandTimedOut,
OutputTooLarge or PipeFailed and exits 1; on wrong arguments the usage,
exit 1.  It is tested against an sshd on 127.0.0.1.
"""
module Wolly.Example.SshRun is
    """
    The command of the arguments.
    No contract: the outcome is the result of I/O.
    """
    function main(root: RootCapability): ExitCode;
end module.
